From 9bcddf85d226a776f9882447cfb1714119e610ae Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 14:32:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 43/59] nouveau/vk: nvkmd_horizon, keep the binding when unbind
 fails

nvkmd_horizon_va_unbind removed the binding from va->bindings, called
horizon_gpu_vm_unmap, freed the binding, and only then looked at the
result.

horizon_gpu_vm_unmap does not tear anything down when it fails -- it
deliberately leaves the mapping object and the kernel mapping alive so
the caller can retry. The binding was the only pointer to that mapping,
and it had already been unlinked and freed by the time the failure was
noticed, so the mapping became unreachable: a later unbind reports
nothing bound at that offset, nvkmd_horizon_va_free stays BUSY forever
because horizon_gpu still counts a live mapping against the range, and
the memory behind it is lost for the lifetime of the process. One failed
unmap was enough to strand a VA range permanently.

Check the result first. On failure the binding goes back on the list and
the caller gets the error with the mapping still tracked and still
unbindable; the FREE happens only on the path where there is nothing
left to point at.

Found by review on PR #6.
---
 .../vulkan/nvkmd/horizon/nvkmd_horizon_va.c    | 18 +++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/nouveau/vulkan/nvkmd/horizon/nvkmd_horizon_va.c b/src/nouveau/vulkan/nvkmd/horizon/nvkmd_horizon_va.c
index 54e53c9..c543c25 100644
--- a/src/nouveau/vulkan/nvkmd/horizon/nvkmd_horizon_va.c
+++ b/src/nouveau/vulkan/nvkmd/horizon/nvkmd_horizon_va.c
@@ -253,14 +253,30 @@ nvkmd_horizon_va_unbind(struct nvkmd_va *_va,
    }
 
    horizon_gpu_result res = horizon_gpu_vm_unmap(found->mapping);
-   FREE(found);
    if (res.status != HORIZON_GPU_OK) {
+      /* horizon_gpu_vm_unmap keeps the mapping object and the kernel
+       * mapping alive when it fails, precisely so the operation can be
+       * retried. Freeing the binding here would throw away the only
+       * pointer to that still-live mapping: the next unbind would
+       * report nothing bound, the VA could never be released because
+       * horizon_gpu still counts the mapping against it, and the memory
+       * behind it would be unreachable for the process's lifetime.
+       *
+       * So it goes back on the list it was taken off, in the same
+       * position-independent way it was found, and the caller gets the
+       * failure with the binding still tracked and still unbindable.
+       */
+      simple_mtx_lock(&va->mutex);
+      list_addtail(&found->link, &va->bindings);
+      simple_mtx_unlock(&va->mutex);
+
       return vk_errorf(log_obj, nvkmd_horizon_result(res),
                        "horizon_gpu_vm_unmap(+0x%" PRIx64 ") failed: "
                        "status %d, nv 0x%08" PRIx32,
                        va_offset_B, (int)res.status, res.nv);
    }
 
+   FREE(found);
    return VK_SUCCESS;
 }
 
